story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Jackson County has a record from 1951 to 2025, and April to May came in under 90% of normal in 34 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle ran 72% of normal in November to December and 143% in June to July. So far in 2026 it sits at 46% for January to February and 163% for May to June. Grid 22977 had its driest year in 1987 at 66% of normal.</p>"}
